cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "handoverloss: three-way attribution of data loss across an optical ground-station handover"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/handoverloss"
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
abstract: >-
  Attributes end-to-end data loss across a ground-station handover on an optical
  downlink separately to acquisition time, protocol restart and buffer drain,
  with an event-level bootstrap interval on each mechanism and a reported
  decomposition residual between two independent accountings of the total. The
  headline output is which of the three mechanisms dominates, which is what tells
  an operator whether to buy faster acquisition, a different protocol or more
  buffer. Includes the acquisition-only assumption implemented at full strength as
  the thing being refuted, an analytic fluid buffer-drain and restart model in
  closed form, direct accounting over a simulated handover trace as ground truth,
  an independently derived bracket on the total from conservation and capacity
  counting alone, and a learned predictor with an uncertainty output scored on
  held-out station pairs and held-out time separately. On the committed synthetic
  corpus the analytic model beats the learned predictor on both held-out splits
  and that result is published rather than retuned. Research-grade; not
  flight-qualified, not certified, and not approved for operational aerospace use.
keywords:
  - optical-communications
  - ground-station-handover
  - acquisition-pointing-tracking
  - fluid-queue
  - loss-attribution
  - bootstrap-confidence-interval
  - network-calculus
